course: dictionary
lesson: 8989
title: One small word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word six can mean different things, and the words around it tell you which one. «At six he said "one more game, the last one".» Here six is a time, like six o'clock, because it is about when something happened.
explain: «Like all insects, a beetle has six legs, three body parts and two feelers.» Here six is a count of things. Six can also count groups: six boxes with four toys in each is 6 × 4, so you multiply the six by the four.
explain: In cricket, a six is a hit worth six runs. In a sentence like «At sixes and sevens» the word six is part of a phrase, and the whole phrase means in a muddle. Always read the whole sentence before you decide what six means.
fact: Six is the number 6, one more than five.
fact: A six is the digit 6, and it can also mean a hit worth six runs in cricket.
fact: «At sixes and sevens» means in a muddle, so the phrase is not about numbers at all.
fact: Six can tell a time, as in «six o'clock», or count things, as in «six ducklings».
exercise: «Nine-year-old Ella Brown rescued six ducklings from a drain on Monday.» How many ducklings did Ella rescue? | Nine | *Six | One | Eleven
exercise: Sam says «at sixes and sevens» means very happy and smiling. What does the phrase really mean? | Very happy | Counting quickly | Playing cricket | *In a muddle
exercise: «Like all insects, a beetle has six legs, three body parts and two feelers.» How many legs does a beetle have? | Four | Eight | Two | *Six
test: «Saffie gets home at quarter to four to an empty house till six.» What time does the word six show? | Six runs | Six ducklings | Six legs | *Six o'clock
test: A dice has how many faces? | *Six | Seven | Five | Four
exam: «The land is split into continents, but how many depends on who is counting: seven in Britain and America, six where one America is taught.» In some places, how many continents are taught? | Seven | Five | Nine | *Six
